# 6. Local Development Architecture

Initially use a single LiveKit server.

Do NOT build a distributed LiveKit cluster.

Local architecture:

```
Local Machine

+-------------------------------+
|                               |
|   Fastify Backend             |
|        |                      |
|        | LiveKit SDK           |
|        |                      |
|        v                      |
|   LiveKit Server              |
|                               |
|   PostgreSQL                   |
|                               |
+-------------------------------+
```

Redis is NOT required for the initial single-node LiveKit deployment.

The existing application Redis can continue to serve application purposes if the project already uses it.

Do not add another Redis dependency solely for LiveKit at this stage.

---

# 7. Why Redis Is Not Needed Initially

A single LiveKit server can operate independently.

Redis becomes important when we run multiple LiveKit nodes.

For example:

```
Load Balancer
     |
+----+----+
|    |    |
v    v    v
```

LK1  LK2  LK3
\    |    /
\   |   /
Redis

Redis is used by distributed LiveKit deployments for shared coordination and messaging.

Redis is NOT part of the audio/video media path.

Do NOT design:

```
User
  |
LiveKit
  |
Redis
  |
LiveKit
  |
User
```

That is incorrect.

The media path is:

```
User
  |
  | WebRTC
  v
LiveKit
  |
  | WebRTC
  v
Other User
```

Redis is a coordination mechanism between LiveKit nodes.

Therefore:

LOCAL:

```
Fastify
   +
LiveKit
   +
PostgreSQL
```

Later, when scaling:

```
Fastify
   +
Load Balancer
   +
Multiple LiveKit nodes
   +
Redis
```

