# 30. Testing Plan

## Test 1 — Server startup

Verify LiveKit starts successfully.

## Test 2 — Fastify token generation

Call:

```
POST /meetings/:meetingId/token
```

Verify:

* authenticated user required
* meeting exists
* membership is checked
* unauthorized users are rejected
* correct LiveKit permissions are generated

## Test 3 — Room connection

Verify the generated token allows joining the correct room.

## Test 4 — Permissions

Test:

```
host
participant
listener/read-only
unauthorized user
```

Verify each receives correct permissions.

## Test 5 — Multiple participants

Test:

```
User A
User B
User C
```

in the same LiveKit room.

## Test 6 — Audio/video

Verify normal WebRTC communication.

## Test 7 — Network restrictions

Test through:

* normal home network
* mobile hotspot
* restrictive network

Verify TURN fallback.

## Test 8 — Server restart

Restart LiveKit and verify expected behavior.

## Test 9 — Token expiration

Verify expired/invalid tokens are rejected.

## Test 10 — Load testing

Only after functional correctness is established.

Benchmark realistic:

* concurrent rooms
* concurrent participants
* publishers
* subscribers
* video resolutions
* network bandwidth
* CPU usage

