# 31. Security Requirements

Never expose:

```
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET
```

to the client.

Never commit:

```
.env
```

or production secrets.

Use secure secret management for AWS production.

Use TLS.

Restrict EC2 SSH access.

Use least-privilege IAM.

Restrict Security Group rules.

Keep LiveKit and OS versions updated.

Separate development and production credentials.

Do not reuse development API secrets in production.

