# 34. Definition of Done

The initial implementation is complete when:

* LiveKit runs locally.
* Fastify can communicate with LiveKit.
* LiveKit credentials are stored securely.
* The backend can generate LiveKit access tokens.
* Meeting authorization is performed using our PostgreSQL data.
* Application roles map correctly to LiveKit permissions.
* Unauthorized users cannot obtain valid meeting tokens.
* Clients can join the appropriate LiveKit room.
* Multiple participants can communicate.
* LiveKit is containerized.
* LiveKit is deployed to AWS EC2.
* DNS works.
* TLS works.
* WebRTC UDP connectivity works.
* WebRTC TCP fallback works.
* TURN works for restrictive networks.
* Fastify works against the AWS LiveKit instance.
* Logs and health monitoring exist.
* Deployment and rollback procedures are documented.

