# 36. Key Principles for Codex

1. Do not implement WebRTC ourselves.
2. Do not embed LiveKit Server inside Fastify.
3. Use LiveKit Server as a separate service/container.
4. Use livekit-server-sdk from Fastify for token generation/API interaction.
5. Never expose LiveKit API secrets to clients.
6. Authenticate users through our own backend.
7. Authorize meeting access through our own database.
8. Map application permissions to LiveKit grants.
9. Do not put audio/video through Fastify.
10. Do not put audio/video through Redis.
11. Do not introduce Redis for LiveKit until distributed deployment is required.
12. Start with one LiveKit node.
13. Develop locally first.
14. Keep local and AWS application logic as similar as possible.
15. Use Docker to make the deployment reproducible.
16. Deploy the first production LiveKit node on AWS EC2.
17. Use DNS + trusted TLS + correct WebRTC networking.
18. Test TURN explicitly.
19. Benchmark before deciding EC2 sizing.
20. Scale to Redis + multiple LiveKit nodes only when actual workload requires it.
21. Do not introduce Kubernetes/EKS prematurely.
22. Follow the current official LiveKit deployment documentation for exact production configuration and port requirements.
23. Reuse the existing project's architecture, authentication, configuration, database, error handling, logging, and testing conventions rather than creating parallel systems.
